# :set on the engine's options, which the IDE keeps in its registry (options.txt, ED-13).

=== :set sw+= adds to a number option
ref:    nvim/options.txt *:set+=*
quote:  Add the {value} to a number option
given:  |x
keys:   :set sw=2 et<CR>:set sw+=2<CR>>>
expect:
  |    x
mode:   normal

=== :set sw-= subtracts from it
ref:    nvim/options.txt *:set-=*
quote:  Subtract the {value} from a number option
given:  |x
keys:   :set sw=6 et<CR>:set sw-=4<CR>>>
expect:
  |  x
mode:   normal

=== :set sw^= multiplies it
ref:    nvim/options.txt *:set^=*
quote:  Multiply the {value} to a number option
given:  |x
keys:   :set sw=3 et<CR>:set sw^=2<CR>>>
expect:
  |      x
mode:   normal

=== :set noet goes back to tabs
ref:    nvim/options.txt *'expandtab'*
quote:  Spaces are used in indents with the '>' and '<' commands
given:  |x
keys:   :set sw=8 et<CR>:set noet<CR>>>
expect:
  |	x
mode:   normal

=== :set ic makes a search ignore case
ref:    nvim/options.txt *'ignorecase'*
quote:  Ignore case in search patterns
given:
  |a
  FOO
keys:   :set ic<CR>/foo<CR>
expect:
  a
  |FOO
mode:   normal
